  "text_excerpt": "SOP:  Process  Code: OPS Date:  01/01/2022 \n Department:  Operations  Addressed to:  Client \n Written by: HOO  Verified by:  Sales | Ops \n Approved by:  COOClient’s SOPs & SLAs \nVersion 1.0 \nContent: \n●Company Concept \n○Who we are ? \n○Fulfillment Process \n○Last Mile Sequence \n○What sets us apart \nfrom the rest ? \n●Onboard Process \n○Onboard Workflow \n○Onboard Procedure. \n○Onboard Exceptions. \n○Prohibited \n●Inbound Process \n○Replenishment \n○Workflow \n○Inbound Procedure ●  Inventory Process \n○Inventory Workflow \n○Inventory Procedure \n○Inventory Exception \n○SLA\n○Prohibited \n●Fulfillment Process \n○Segregation of Orders \n○B2C Procedure \n●  Outbound Process \n○Outbound Workflow \n○Outbound Procedure \n○Outbound Exceptions \n○SLA\n○Prohibited ●Exceptions | Module \n○Before Adding to Inventory \n○Before Receiving the Orders \n○Before Assigning to Picker \n○Before Order Packaging \n○Before Order Dispatching \n○Financial Module for \nCompanies \n●  Closing Account Process \n○Workflow \n○SLA\n○Prohibited \n●Client Forecast \n○Workflow \n○Forecast Procedure \n○Prohibited ●  Return Process \n○Workflow \n○Return Procedure \n○Exception \n○SLA\n○Prohibited \n●  Special Process 3PL \n○SLA\n○Prohibited \n\n\n\n\nOnboard Process: \n●This step describes how you will be onboarded to grow your business. Our system is capable of \nauto-product creation through our integration once you list your product in your website. However, it \nis important to review your new listed product under Product Management to avoid any missing \ninformation. \nOnboard Workflow: \nAccount \nCreation Data \nSubmissio nSystem \nIntegration System \nTraining Create \nASN Create \nManifest  Receiving \nProduct \nDetails         Product \n        Details Product \nCreation Product \nDetails  Product \n Image 1.1.1 1.1.2 1.1.3 1.1.4 1.1.5 1.1.9 1.1.10 \n1.1.7 1.1.8 1.1.6 \n● Account Creation:  After signing the contract our team will create an account for you in our system. \n● Data Submission:  The client must upload the products or he should provide file to our team  to fill in your products list \nand in this file we will need data for each product. \n● System Integration:  The client must inform about their platform and tech will integrate with DIGGIPACKS. \n● System Training:  Our talented team will meet you to train you on using our system. \n● Create ASN: \n○Create Replenishment. \n○Import the file from the portal and fill the required product details and upload in one time. \n○Upload the Zip file contains images with SKU code and upload. \n○Create manifest for the products which you want to drop at our facility else pick up from your location. \n○All the products should be received with Labelling (Barcoding) else DIGGIPACKS will do it with an additional charge. \n\u0000To maintain faster receiving: \n\u0000Print Manifest from Client Portal and attach with your shipment. \n\u0000Palletized your shipment. \n\u0000Put your SKUs in boxes (Each SKU in a box is highly recommended). \n\u0000Product Creation:  In case there is missing product is not added or you wish to add new product to your selection so the \nnew manifest will be created. \n\u0000Product Images: Mandatory to upload your product images to ensure improve Operations quality work and eliminate \nany errors or DIGGIPACKS will take the picture of your products to upload with an additional charge. \nOnboard Procedure \nOnboard Exceptions: \n●In case client prefer to not do the system integration. Then, client \nwill have to use our Client Portal for manual process. \nProhibited: \n►In case you have expiry product, then you need to mention the expiry \ndate while creating manifest, this will allow our team to arrange your \nproduct in the FIFO manner. \n\nInbound: \n●This section describes usual process for receiving your products. \nReplenishment: \n► You should make manifest through the client portal from your side so we can compare \nexpected QTYs & arrived or received QTYs. \nWorkflow: \nPushing \nManifest \nBins / Storage \n Schedule\n pickup from\nClient Portal\n Receiving with\n QC\n Inventory with\nBarcoding\nSubmittedShelves / ...",
